👇 READ BELOW for what it does and how to use it

It’s a free, open source Claude Code skill with over 17,000 stars on GitHub.

1️⃣ Paste any video link
YouTube, Loom, TikTok, Instagram, X, Vimeo and a few hundred more sites. Local video files work too.

2️⃣ Ask it anything
Type /watch, paste the link, then your question. “What hook did they open with?” is a great first one.

3️⃣ It actually watches
It pulls a frame from every scene change plus a timestamped transcript, then Claude reads every frame as an image.

What people use it for:

Breaking down a viral video’s hook, second by second.

Finding the exact frame where a bug shows up in a screen recording.

Turning a long tutorial into notes, or into a custom skill you can reuse in Claude or ChatGPT.

Good to know: captions are free and cover most public videos. You only need a Whisper API key when a video has no captions.

Save this for your next research session.

